### Read-off Method and Precision

Forward read: locate the specified x on the calibrated horizontal scale,
subdivide a .05 cell only approximately when needed, project vertically to
the ORIGINAL solid curve, and horizontally to the y scale.
Inverse read: locate the specified positive y on the vertical scale,
project horizontally to the solid curve and vertically to the x scale.
All directly read queries have x in [0,1] or y in [1,10].
For other exponents, shift by an exact integral power of ten; do not extrapolate
the drawn curve beyond its source endpoints.

Coarse useful reporting: about a tenth in y and about a hundredth or a few
hundredths in x. The last reported digit is not uniquely warranted by this
hand-drawn coarse scan. The descriptive bands below are observational
read-off latitude, NOT certified interval bounds or a grading-tolerance contract.
Adjacent reported values such as 1.7/1.8 or .18/.20 can be compatible with
the same scan. No nearest-.01-y or nearest-.001-x requirement is invented.
Digits in a given such as .865, .584, 6.2, or 9.37 do not increase graph precision.

