### 665 -- Two Groups, Eight Quantities

Input binding: /exercises/0; g0; pages p0220#7 and p0221#1; explicit fig-82.
Task: use the graph of y=10^x.
a: given x=.1,.25,.72,.865, determine 10^x.
b: given 10^x=3,5,6.2,9.37, determine x.

a: using the four forward projections recorded above, one suitable approximate
tuple is (1.3,1.8,5.2,7.3), in exactly the source order. Every entry is an
APPROXIMATION; alternatives within the recorded graph latitude are not uniquely
falsified by the source scan. Do not write exact equality to this tuple.

b: using the four inverse projections, one suitable approximate tuple is
(.48,.70,.79,.97). Each positive target lies between 1 and 10, so the unique
exact exponent lies between 0 and 1. Completeness follows from strict increase,
not from simply finding one visible intersection.

